{
  "title": "Greetings and courtesy",
  "note": "Greetings change with the time of day and the setting. In こんにちは and こんばんは the final は is read wa. Polite forms end in ございます or します; shortened ありがとう and おはよう sound casual. さん after a name means Mr. or Ms., but never use it with your own name.",
  "src": {
    "t": "IRODORI: Japanese for Life in Japan (Starter), The Japan Foundation",
    "u": "https://www.irodori.jpf.go.jp/en/"
  },
